course: dictionary
lesson: 3642
title: One word, many fires
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one the writer means. In «a house fire», fire means a burning that destroys something. In «fire a rocket», fire is a verb meaning to shoot or send something off. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence best.
explain: Look at the words near the word. «The Mole woke with a start when a coal slipped and the fire crackled» tells you fire is the flames and heat that come from burning, because it crackles and sends up a spurt of flame. A campfire is a small fire made on purpose, so the clues about camping and warmth would point you to that meaning.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If you read «A bombardier beetle shoots a boiling puff» and it still makes sense, then fire means shoots. If it does not make sense, try another meaning until it does.
fact: Fire can be a noun, meaning the flames and heat, or a verb, meaning to shoot or to tell someone they no longer have their job.
fact: «A house fire» means a burning that destroys something, and «a campfire» means a small fire made on purpose for warmth or cooking.
fact: A fire needs three things: heat, fuel and oxygen. This is called the fire triangle, and if you take one away, the fire goes out.
fact: «Caught fire» means started to burn, and «set fire to» means to make something start burning.
fact: If there is a fire, get out, stay out and call your local emergency number: 911, 999, 000, 111 or 112, depending on where you live.
exercise: «A family left a pan of oil on the hob and it caught fire.» What does caught fire mean? | *Started to burn | Was cooked very quickly | Was put out with water
exercise: «A bombardier beetle fires a boiling puff with a pop.» What does fires mean here? | Lights a small campfire | *Shoots or sends out | Gets a new job | Stops working
exercise: Her boss told Sam he was being fired. What does fired mean? | Asked to make a fire | *Told he no longer has his job | Given a prize | Sent up like a rocket
test: What is a campfire? | A fire made by accident in a house | *A small fire made on purpose for warmth or cooking | A gun that fires rockets
test: In the fire triangle, what three things does a fire need? | Metal, paper and glass | Smoke, ash and sparks | Water, sand and wind | *Heat, fuel and oxygen
exam: If your clothes catch fire, what should you do? | Open a window and wave your arms | Hide under the bed until it is over | *Stop, drop and roll | Run around the room as fast as you can
